  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "instruction",
      "text": "Principle 13. Who I respect (1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "161",
          "text": "When I was young my mother would read to me before I went to bed."
        },
        {
          "n": "162",
          "text": "She made me read a lot and I enjoyed them."
        },
        {
          "n": "163",
          "text": "I like fiction, history and books about other countries."
        },
        {
          "n": "164",
          "text": "But I especially like history books because I can read about the wisdom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "of many people."
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "165",
          "text": "I have read about many interesting people in history books."
        },
        {
          "n": "166",
          "text": "I admire some of them."
        },
        {
          "n": "167",
          "text": "The person I respect the most is General Lee Soon-sin."
        },
        {
          "n": "168",
          "text": "General Lee lived 500 years ago."
        },
        {
          "n": "169",
          "text": "He made a Turtle ship and defeated Japan."
        },
        {
          "n": "170",
          "text": "I respect him because he prepared well and he always thought of Korea"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "before himself."
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "171",
          "text": "As well he always tried to complete his responsibilities."
        }
      ]
    },
